1
00:00:00,299 --> 00:00:04,181
This is our ESP32 quadcopter
control prototype.

2
00:00:04,779 --> 00:00:06,187
The OLED displays its state,

3
00:00:06,613 --> 00:00:11,349
while an MPU6050 measures
acceleration and angular rate.

4
00:00:11,972 --> 00:00:16,110
The controller estimates roll and pitch,
compares both with zero degrees,

5
00:00:16,665 --> 00:00:19,652
then mixes corrections into
four ESC commands.

6
00:00:20,334 --> 00:00:23,791
Here, the dashboard adjusts motor output
and plots the response.

7
00:00:24,716 --> 00:00:27,362
The reported gains are P: one point five,

8
00:00:27,874 --> 00:00:31,415
I: zero, and D: zero point zero five,

9
00:00:31,884 --> 00:00:33,079
so this is P D control.

10
00:00:33,932 --> 00:00:36,194
The loop is scheduled every
ten milliseconds.

11
00:00:36,765 --> 00:00:39,325
The motor test demonstrates
the prototype hardware;

12
00:00:39,837 --> 00:00:44,061
stable hover and automatic altitude hold
still require separate validation.
